{{Quote|Cadets, you are descending into the Well and must climb out with all deliberate speed. You will be given the honor of serving as aides in the Imperial Headquarters. Those who lose will be serving Taskmaster Grint and wish they'd stayed at the bottom of that Well.|Cumberlayne Aresko prepares the cadets for the challenge|<ref name="Breaking Ranks">{{Rebels|Breaking Ranks}}</ref>}}
'''The Well''' was a purpose-built facility at [[Lothal]]'s [[Academy for Young Imperials]] which could be remotely configured to simulate a wide variety of obstacle courses and challenges. It was a large artificial pit that could automatically descend to a certain depth. Its walls were flanked by automated [[repulsorlift]] platforms that were used by the cadets to climb back to the top. It could sometimes be remotely configured to include the [[Pillar]], a towering structure that the cadets were required to climb.<ref name="Breaking Ranks" />

The Well was used by [[Commandant]] [[Cumberlayne Aresko]] to instill the importance of achieving victory at all costs among the cadets. Aresko also rewarded the top three winners with extra rations, work details at the [[Imperial Complex (Lothal)|Imperial Complex]], and even a ride on an [[All Terrain Defense Pod|AT-DP walker]]. He also used the Well to assess the physical prowess, mental acuity, leadership skills, and strategic adaptability of the [[Imperial cadet]]s. While [[Mission to destroy a kyber crystal|infiltrating]] the Imperial Academy, the [[Spectres|rebel]] [[Ezra Bridger]] trained with fellow cadets [[Jai Kell]] and [[Zare Leonis]] on several occasions in the Well.<ref name="Breaking Ranks" />

